#
# Conformance case: foundation/exactly-one-stereotype
# AC: foundation lowering — OntoUML StereotypeCardinality discipline (issue #503).
#
# Reproduces reasoning_lint.exactly_one_stereotype: a class must carry EXACTLY
# one logic: stereotype. Two offenders, both tripping logic:StereotypeCardinality:
#   * ex:NoStereo  — appears in a logic:subClassOf edge (so it is a class) but
#     carries NO stereotype pun at all → StereotypeCardinality (the 0-branch).
#   * ex:TwoStereo — carries TWO stereotypes (logic:Kind AND logic:Role) →
#     StereotypeCardinality (the >1-branch). It is ALSO an anti-rigid sortal
#     (Role) with no rigid ancestor, so it additionally trips logic:FreeRole —
#     the FULL lint set, faithfully reproduced (anti_rigidity_discipline fires
#     independently of exactly_one_stereotype).
# ex:Anchor is a clean top logic:Kind (carries exactly one stereotype, no parent)
# and trips nothing — the negative control.
#
# CRITICAL: the chase seeds only from input.nq world facts, so the schema facts
# (stereotype rdf:type puns + logic:subClassOf) are duplicated there in the named
# world ex:schema; these declarations are the program axioms the projections need.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/foundation/exactly-one-stereotype/> .
@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# Schema: stereotype puns + subsumption (also asserted as world facts in input.nq).
ex:Anchor    a logic:Kind .
ex:TwoStereo a logic:Kind, logic:Role .
ex:NoStereo  logic:subClassOf ex:Anchor .
